Suppose $Y\to B$ is relatively weakly mixing for $R$. For distinct nonzero integers $a_1,\ldots,a_d$ and bounded $G_1,\ldots,G_d$, $$\label{eq:relative-norm}
 \left\|\frac1N\sum_{l=1}^N
 \left(\prod_{i=1}^dG_i\circ R^{a_il}
       -\prod_{i=1}^d\mathbb E[G_i\mid B]\circ R^{a_il}\right)\right\|_2
 \longrightarrow0.$$

There are a finite set $F\subseteq[1,2]$ containing $1$ and measurable functions $N_a:C\to[2^a,\infty)$, $a\in\mathbb N$, independent of the phase, with $$\label{eq:selector-grid}
  N_a(x,u)\in\{c2^k:c\in F,\ k\ge a\},\qquad
  N_a(x,u)=2^a\quad(x\notin E_*),$$ such that $B_{\lfloor N_a(x,u)\rfloor}(x)>\delta$ on $E_*$. Moreover, there is a continuous nonnegative function $\Psi$ on $(\mathbb R/\mathbb Z)^I$ for which $$\label{eq:selected-positive-limit}
 \liminf_{a\to\infty}\int_C\frac1{N_a(z)}
 \int_0^{N_a(z)}
 \Psi\bigl((\upsilon(S_C^{it}z))_{i\in I}\bigr)
 \prod_{i\in J_0}f_i\bigl(\xi(S_C^{it}z)\bigr)
 \,\,dt\,\,dm_C(z)>0.$$

Every flow $Y$ over $C$ has a unique probability law $\lambda_Y$ on $Y^I$ satisfying, for all bounded measurable functions $G_i$ on $Y$, $$\label{eq:selected-law}
 \int_{Y^I}\prod_{i\in I}G_i(y_i)\,\,d\lambda_Y
 =\lim_{a\to\mathcal U}\int_Y\frac1{N_a(\pi_Yy)}
   \int_0^{N_a(\pi_Yy)}\prod_{i\in I}G_i(S_Y^{it}y)
   \,\,dt\,\,dm_Y(y).$$ Its marginals are $m_Y$, and it is invariant under $(y_i)_i\mapsto(S_Y^{it}y_i)_i$, $t\in\mathbb R$. If $\rho:Y'\to Y$ is an extension over $C$, then $(\rho^I)_*\lambda_{Y'}=\lambda_Y$.*

*Countable inverse limits of extensions over $C$ exist in this category. The selected law at such a limit projects to the selected law at every stage. Pullbacks of the stage selected-law spaces have dense union in $L^2$ of the limit selected law.

With the functions and phase test of Lemma <a href="#lem:selected-witness" data-reference-type="ref" data-reference="lem:selected-witness">7</a>, $$\label{eq:positive-witness}
 \int_{C^I}\Psi\bigl((\upsilon(z_i))_i\bigr)
    \prod_{i\in J_0}f_i\bigl(\xi(z_i)\bigr)\,\,d\lambda_C>0.$$ The phase array in this integral is measurable in the distal parameter array of $C^I$.

There is a universal constant $C$ with the following property. Let $0<\varepsilon\le1$, and let $d\ge1$ and $L\ge0$ be integers. Let $x_1,\ldots,x_m$ and $y_1,\ldots,y_m$ lie in the unit balls of real Hilbert spaces $H_1,H_2$. For each family suppose that a graph on $\{1,\ldots,m\}$ of maximum degree at most $L$ contains every off-diagonal pair whose absolute inner product exceeds $\eta$, where $$0\le\eta\le\varepsilon^2/10^4.$$ The two exceptional graphs may differ. For every orthogonal projection $P$ on $H_1\otimes H_2$ of rank at most $d$, $$\label{eq:packing-quantitative}
 \#\{j:\lVert P(x_j\otimes y_j)\rVert\ge\varepsilon\}
 \le C(1+L)\varepsilon^{-2}
       \exp\!\left(C\varepsilon^{-2}\sqrt d\log(2+d)\right).$$ For $d=d_m$ as defined in <a href="#eq:channel-dimension" data-reference-type="eqref" data-reference="eq:channel-dimension">[eq:channel-dimension]</a>, this is $o_{\varepsilon,L}(m)$, uniformly over the Hilbert spaces, vectors, projections, and allowed values of $\eta$.

Let $B_1,\ldots,B_r$ be matrices between two finite-dimensional real Hilbert spaces, and put $$H_j=\begin{pmatrix}0&B_j\\B_j^*&0\end{pmatrix},
 \qquad S=\sum_{j=1}^rH_j^2.$$ If $\lVert S\rVert_{\rm op}\le\sqrt d$ and $\mathop{\mathrm{tr}}S\le2d$ for some $d\ge1$, then for independent standard normal variables $g_j$, $$\label{eq:packing-gaussian-bound}
 \mathbb E\left\|\sum_{j=1}^rg_jB_j\right\|_{\rm op}
       \le C d^{1/4}\sqrt{\log(2+d)}.$$ The constant is independent of the dimensions of the two spaces.
